# AI discovery crawl (always)

Resume: `@crawl$` / `$discovery$`.

Master Admin → **AI Crawling**. Internet search (Google Places + public pages today) → parse → human review → approve → live `clubLocations` / `events`. Ticketmaster Discovery API confirmation is **later**.

## Operator UX contract (non-technical)

- Approval is driven by **named form fields** and a Pass/Missing checklist — never by editing JSON.
- Raw/parsed payloads are **Advanced** only. Labels: “Source snapshot” / “What FLOQR understood” — not “JSON”.
- Rating criteria use **number inputs** (weights). Machine dump stays under Advanced.
- Profile import: **Prepare Club Admin imports** → review cards → Save drafts / send link. Advanced “generated data” disclosure is optional.
- Source Detail Extraction is a **wizard**: one event/venue detail URL (not a search-results list) → extract → save.
- Queue actions: **Approve** | **Needs research** | Reject | Duplicate | Delete.
- **Mass onboard:** select ready cards (all required datapoints present) → **Onboard selected**. Not-ready cards stay listed with **Missing datapoints** called out; they cannot be selected for mass publish.

## Schedule (defaults)

| Control | Default |
|---|---|
| Runs / day | 6 (live `aiCrawlerSchedules/default`) |
| Slots | `00:00`, `04:00`, `08:00`, `12:00`, `16:00`, `20:00` |
| Time zone | `UTC` on live schedule doc (design default was `America/New_York`) |
| Focus | Spain + Germany · Hip Hop · concert / nightclub / club / lounge |
| Language | Native market + English |

Backend: `scheduledAiDiscoveryCrawl` every **15 minutes UTC**; runs when local time is within 15 minutes of a saved slot; claims `aiCrawlRuns/{scheduleId}_{slot}`. Saved in `aiCrawlerSchedules/default`.

**UI load pitfall:** Master Admin must read `aiCrawlRuns` with `orderBy(startedAt, desc)` and `aiDiscoveryQueue` with `orderBy(createdAt, desc)`. An unordered `.limit(N)` returns document-id order, so run ids like `default_2026-07-*` fill the page and the newest successful slot (still writing in Sept+) never appears — operators report a false “last crawl July 28.”

Manual **Run Discovery Crawl** / **Instant Crawl Now** call `runFloqrDiscoveryCrawl` / `runInstantDiscoveryCrawl`. Instant uses the saved `aiCrawlerSchedules/default` (or form criteria), caps jobs (~8), and returns contact-lift stats (Phone+Email+Instagram before/after website enrich). On failure: **fail loudly** — do **not** seed placeholder search-plan review cards.

**Social / contact enrichment:** Prefer `href` / JSON-LD `sameAs` / `mailto:` / `tel:` / `wa.me` over visible text. Rank Instagram/Facebook handles against the venue name + website host so photographer credit links lose to `@gateclubparis`. Penalize aggregator chrome (`privateaser`, marketplace emails). When Places `websiteUri` is an aggregator (Privateaser, OpenTable, TheFork, TripAdvisor, Yelp, RA/Dice/Shotgun/Eventbrite, Linktree, Paris Society), always follow linked official brand domains and re-rank Facebook/email even if Instagram was already filled. When Instagram or email/phone is still missing, follow up to **4** same-origin secondary pages (contact, privatisation, about, réseaux) — never CSS/JS/wp-content assets. **Do not scrape Facebook.com** (login walls); collect Facebook URLs only when the venue website links them.

## Collections

| Collection | Role |
|---|---|
| `aiCrawlerSchedules` | Enabled schedule + criteria + structured plan |
| `aiCrawlRuns` | Manual / scheduled run lifecycle |
| `aiDiscoveryQueue` | Review-only candidates (+ `profile-import-draft`) |
